#   ---- H22 and H24. coinductive typing: the ghost certificate ----
#
#   Ported from MIXINv8's typed natural (`MIXINv8/prolog/mixinv8/types/
#   builtin/natural.pl`) without its premise, and in its idiom: the
#   judgment answers a CERTIFICATE, a package whose `identity` member is
#   the identity function, and a method uses the judgment as a CHANNEL,
#   passing its payload through the certificate's identity, so that an
#   argument that fails the judgment leaves the method's answer with no
#   head at all ("THE GATE IS A CHANNEL, NOT A MARK", natural.pl). For a
#   subject whose tag is false the else branch equates `J x` with `(J x)
#   (\i. \w. w)`: an equation other values satisfy, but no certificate,
#   since a certificate is not its own second member.
#
#   An object is a Scott triple (tag, method, base): `tag` a Scott
#   boolean, the object's claim to be a natural; `method` its `add`,
#   taking an object and answering one; `base` a Scott boolean, true for an
#   object the judgment certifies without looking further (none is built
#   in these points). The judgment and the members:
#
#       certificate = \sel. sel (\x. x) (\a. \b. \c. c)
#       identity_of = \package. package (\i. \w. i)
#       J x         = (tag x) ((base x) certificate (J (method x member))) ((J x) (\i. \w. w))
#       symbol      = (true, \that. (identity_of (J that)) symbol, false)
#
#   `J symbol` needs `J (method symbol symbol)`, and `method symbol
#   symbol` is `(identity_of (J symbol)) symbol`, which applies the value
#   of `J symbol`. Its least solution gives no head
#   (a tabled reading `failed`). The certificate is a solution: assumed
#   for `J symbol`, `identity_of certificate` is the identity, the method
#   answers `symbol`, and the judgment comes back to `J` of a term whose
#   value is `symbol`'s, every judgment on the chain answering the
#   assumed certificate. The claim is that the certificate is
#   in the answer set, `some_solution(certificate(natural))`,
#   compared as a term: MIXINv8 asks whether that very
#   certificate is obtained, not whether the answer set is non-empty,
#   and other ghost solutions of the cycle are irrelevant to it. The
#   certificate's code occurs in the program only as the certificate
#   itself (`\sel. sel (\x. x) (\a. \b. \c. c)`); a closure of the same
#   code elsewhere would be the same certificate, since codes are content
#   addressed where MIXINv8's anchors are nominal.
#
#   ONE STATE FOR THE MEMBER. The derivation needs the member the root
#   judges and the member the judgment's body passes to the method to be
#   one term, and the judgment the member's method calls to be the
#   judgment being computed. Both recursions are therefore tied as a
#   self-application `W W` with `W = \p. G (p p)`, never as `fixpoint G`,
#   and the root binds J once, `(\judge. judge (member over judge)) J`.
#   Each W is built by its own call, so the two copies are alpha
#   equivalent and share no binder.
